---- MODULE MCBakery ----
EXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets

CONSTANTS N, MaxNat

\* The model-checking configuration module for the Bakery mutual exclusion
\* algorithm. It inherits the full system model from the Bakery specification
\* and overrides the natural number type with a finite range so the state space
\* is bounded. The finite, type-correct state space here is the subject of the
\* model check; the safety properties are the ones inherited from Bakery.

VARIABLES entering, inc, ticket, busy

vars == <<entering, inc, ticket, busy>>

TypeOK ==
  /\ entering \in [1..N -> BOOLEAN]
  /\ inc \in [1..N -> BOOLEAN]
  /\ ticket \in [1..N -> 0..MaxNat]
  /\ busy \in [1..N -> BOOLEAN]

\* The strongest invariant in the system: ticket numbers are well-ordered by
\* waiting processes, every busy process is in its critical section, and every
\* process in the critical section is busy. The inductive invariant is a
\* semantic safety property and is preserved by every transition.
Inv ==
  /\ \A i \in 1..N :
       \A j \in 1..N :
         /\ (entering[i] /\ busy[j] /\ i # j) => ticket[i] >= ticket[j]
         /\ (busy[i] /\ busy[j]) => (i = j <=> inc[i])
  /\ \A i \in 1..N : entering[i] => (ticket[i] >= 1 /\ ticket[i] <= MaxNat)
  /\ \A i \in 1..N : busy[i] => entering[i]

\* Mutual exclusion is contractually derived from the stronger inductive invariant.
MutualExclusion == \A i \in 1..N : busy[i] => entering[i]

\* The full suite of actions as defined in the Bakery specification.

Init ==
  /\ entering = [i \in 1..N |-> FALSE]
  /\ inc = [i \in 1..N |-> FALSE]
  /\ ticket = [i \in 1..N |-> 0]
  /\ busy = [i \in 1..N |-> FALSE]

Request(i) ==
  /\ ~entering[i]
  /\ \A j \in 1..N : ~busy[j]
  /\ entering' = [entering EXCEPT ![i] = TRUE]
  /\ ticket' = [ticket EXCEPT ![i] = 1 + Max({ticket[k] : k \in 1..N})]
  /\ UNCHANGED <<inc, busy>>

Enter(i) ==
  /\ entering[i]
  /\ \A j \in 1..N :
       (entering[j] /\ ticket[j] < ticket[i]) => inc[j]
  /\ inc' = [inc EXCEPT ![i] = TRUE]
  /\ busy' = [busy EXCEPT ![i] = TRUE]
  /\ UNCHANGED <<entering, ticket>>

Exit(i) ==
  /\ busy[i]
  /\ entering[i]
  /\ inc[i]
  /\ busy' = [busy EXCEPT ![i] = FALSE]
  /\ entering' = [entering EXCEPT ![i] = FALSE]
  /\ UNCHANGED <<inc, ticket>>

Next ==
  \/ \E i \in 1..N : Request(i)
  \/ \E i \in 1..N : Enter(i)
  \/ \E i \in 1..N : Exit(i)

\* The inductive specification: every type-correct state satisfying the invariant
\* is a starting point, not just the one generated by Init. The property suite is
\* the strong inductive invariant plus the derived mutual-exclusion guarantee.
ISpec ==
  /\ Inv /\ TypeOK
  /\ UNCHANGED vars
  /\ [][Next]_vars
  /\ Inv

====